# Copy this whole file ONCE into backend\.env :
#   copy terrametric-laptop.env.example .env
#
# ─── WHAT EACH LINE MEANS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HARDWARE_PI_BASE — URL of the HARDWARE AGENT running ON THE RASPBERRY PI.
#   Bench Pi on this LAN: 10.4.247.246 (wired). Value below must ping from the laptop.
#   • It is NOT your Bluetooth module MAC (those colons belong in HC-05 / bridge,
#     not here). Wrong example: http://00:EE:...
#   • Laptop wired to Pi (Ethernet cable or USB tether / “RNDIS Ethernet”)? Use each
#     machine’s IPv4 ON THAT SAME LINK—not Wi‑Fi addresses. On Pi: hostname -I or
#     ip -4 addr show. On Windows: ipconfig, pick the Ethernet / USB NIC’s IPv4.
#   • Else (Pi on Wi‑Fi/router): ping the Pi hostname or check the router’s DHCP list.
#
# HARDWARE_PI_KEY — shared secret between laptop and Pi hardware agent ONLY.
#   • Must equal DEVICE_KEY exactly in the Pi’s .env next to hardware_agent /
#     start_terrametric_pi.sh pipeline.
#
# SECRET_KEY — signs web login JWTs on the laptop backend (not Pi auth).
#
# On the Pi’s .env — arduino_bridge must reach this laptop (uvicorn on port 8000):
#   TM_BRIDGE_API=http://10.3.25.73:8000
#

HARDWARE_PI_BASE=http://10.4.247.246:8765HARDWARE_PI_KEY=REPLACE_SAME_AS_PI_DEVICE_KEY
SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_LONG_RANDOM_STRING
